codex
The mandatory local gates are green: 37 focused tests and strict mypy over 63 files. The blocking issue remains because the new tests only monkeypatch `sys.platform` and `os.rename`; they execute Darwin’s `chmod` behavior, so they do not cover Linux’s documented unsupported no-follow combination or its cleanup path. I’m completing the full regression gate before recording the rework verdict.
