EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260729-3dr6hw_diagnose-install-race-timeouts/progress.md:42:Read-only diagnosis, no Go command executed (task boundary). Findings: both timeouts are cumulative duration, not deadlock; no DATA RACE marker in the 320-line race log. All three CPU-runnable goroutines in both alarm dumps sit in the same leaf: transaction.namespaceComponents <- namespaceContains <- namespacePathsOverlap <- validateIndependentTargetNamespaces <- Engine.saveJournal <- stageTarget/copyStagingFile. saveJournal validates the target-namespace graph twice per journal write (journal.go:344 and :354), O(targets^2) with EvalSymlinks/Pathconf/Statfs per path plus APFS NFD normalization per component, and fires 3x per staging entry and 2x per 32KiB chunk. Target counts read off the dump frames: 8 for internal/install, 19-20 for the two atomicity scenarios. Because the fault injects at PointAfterBackup (commit phase), every injection first runs a complete Prepare, so injection cost is class-independent and chain length is the only test-only lever. Derived race factor 2.69x (internal/install) and 2.75x (atomicity) from two independent derivations; projections 918s and 1121s against the unchanged 600s alarm. Recommended smallest test-only patch: (A) t.Parallel on exactly 88 of 107 internal/install tests, with 19 excluded by name - 11 t.Setenv, 7 assigning the package-level afterDocumentOpen hook (generation.go:57, read unsynchronized at :81), 1 re-exec child; (B) partition the atomicity sweep to one class per scenario (chain 9->3 project, 7->3 global) with 5 distinct global user homes preserving the sharedUserHome non-overlap invariant, plus t.Parallel on the 7 non-sweep top-level tests. Projected 219-319s and 382-450s. No assertion removed: residue is already asserted directly by before.diff(snapshotState) at commit_atomicity_test.go:178. Out of scope but recorded: the cheap real fix is production-side (hoist namespace validation out of saveJournal or memoize per journal) - routed as a separate story, not smuggled into a test-only rework. Residual risk: parallelizing 88 tests exercises production code concurrently for the first time; a new DATA RACE would be a genuine defect, not a reason to revert. Outcome resource: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md. Logbook entry 2026-07-29 1659.
