Verdict: **changes requested**. `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` is routed to `to-dev`.

The mode-`0000` recovery calls `os.chmod(..., dir_fd=..., follow_symlinks=False)` at [cache_posix.py:1315](/Users/iv/Developer/Wildberries/cocoaskills/.temp/TASK-260720-2jfnz6/worktree/src/csk/builds/cache_posix.py:1315), but unsupported Linux `fchmodat` implementations produce `ValueError`. `_move_aside` only cleans reservations for `OSError`, so a diagnostic reproduced `ValueError` with one leaked reservation. Python documents this combination as platform-dependent, and GNU records `ENOTSUP` on glibc 2.31. [Python documentation](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.chmod), [CPython implementation](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.11.15/Modules/posixmodule.c#L3120-L3177), [GNU portability note](https://www.gnu.org/software/gnulib/manual/html_node/fchmodat.html).

The new tests at [test_build_cache_posix.py:698](/Users/iv/Developer/Wildberries/cocoaskills/.temp/TASK-260720-2jfnz6/worktree/tests/test_build_cache_posix.py:698) emulate Linux rename semantics but still use Darwin’s `chmod` behavior.

